# Superpowers Routing

Use installed Superpowers skills as the primary workflow layer for **non-trivial** work. [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) defines priority when skills conflict with project policy.

**Simple tasks:** implement directly — no skill invocation, no spec/plan gate. See AGENTS.md “Simple tasks”. Escalate when scope, risk, or ambiguity grows.

## Skill routing

| User intent | Required flow |
|-------------|----------------|
| Spec/plan decisions with user | `grill-me` (one question at a time; explore codebase when answer is there) |
| New feature / behavior / architecture change | `brainstorming` → `grill-me` → spec in `docs/superpowers/specs/` |
| Approved design or spec exists | `writing-plans` → `grill-me` for open items → plan in `docs/superpowers/plans/` |
| Plan exists; implementation starts | `executing-plans` or `subagent-driven-development` |
| Bug / regression / failing test | `systematic-debugging` |
| Code change needing regression guard | `test-driven-development` only for **meaningful** coverage (see AGENTS.md Testing) |
| Review requested | `requesting-code-review` |
| Approved plan fully implemented | `finishing-a-development-branch` **then** `babysit` if PR in play |

## Rules

- Do not skip design/spec/planning gates for **non-trivial** work; simple tasks may skip Superpowers entirely.
- **Plan scope freeze:** when plan tasks are done, stop — no C-2/C-3 scope creep without new spec/plan cycle.
- If the user says design is already approved, locate the spec/plan file before coding.
- Persona briefings run **immediately before** implementation; they do not replace brainstorming, `grill-me`, or writing-plans.
- Default communication: `/caveman` (see AGENTS.md).
- Do not modify Superpowers plugin/skills source in this repo.
